  "findings": {
    "U40": "Camp and equipped spell icons show authored modifier art from installed rune IDs, including repeated runes; full spell art stays intact. Equipped tooltip and inventory plain text preserve rune names. Camp markers use the space below price text.",
    "U41": "Entering either constructor selects combined relevant inventory and shop categories, including keystones/runes/finished spells or blueprints/materials/dismantlable equipment/enchantment spells. Native manual filters remain available. Both weapon and armour families share the item constructor.",
    "U42": "A captured shop/bag item repeats after 0.5s at most once per 0.075s tick. Capture keeps full wear/charge ID and stops on release, stock/inventory exhaustion, focus loss, hide, mode/filter/hero/shop change, cancellation or trade submission. Mouse and touch input path assertions pass; trade stays one authority transaction.",
    "U43": "Original LITEM Material contains a placeholder period. MATERIAL <name> carries the actual localized description. Flavor lookup now prioritizes that material record, matching the existing title lookup."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Linux focused fixture validation; no physical gamepad/touch-device or Windows/macOS runtime acceptance. No release or installation.",
    "Existing real ENet regression covers private guest inventory, stacked offers, and atomic validation. Held input is checked through live mouse/touch UI in single-session fixtures; extended internet latency and simultaneous held peer gestures were not separately exercised.",
    "Russian rendered run emits Unicode-to-ASCII diagnostics while its checked strings and localized screenshots remain correct. This work does not claim to fix those diagnostics."
  ],
  "iteration_notes": [
    "build01 passed base 80 checks; visual inspection caught rune/price overlap. build02 moves markers below camp prices and passed base rendered 81 checks (screenshots retained). build03 also restores installed-rune text in tooltips/plain info.",
    "Early LiA fixture used absent bz2g and dereferenced null world in the release runtime (SIGSEGV). Corrected to authored bz1h and guarded absent world; no production/runtime fix inferred. Headless fixture frame waits were fixed before the final 91-check run.",
    "Full-size build03 Russian screenshot review exposed initial completed spell cards hidden by opaque empty legacy 3D viewports. build04 hides empty/spell-piece ItemViews, with a new invariant assertion, base headless 88/88 and Russian rendered 92/92; all three new screenshots inspected and spell card artwork visible. Earlier build03 screenshot records remain as iteration evidence, not final visual acceptance."
  ],
